# A page that is showing while its next address hasn't answered yet (a link clicked on a slow
# site: "Still waiting for … to respond") can still be captured, and the capture sent to an
# easel: the capture menu's New Easel opens the easel instead of never coming back.
# ${STALL} accepts connections and never answers one.
budget rss=800 stalls50=20

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=shown
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://navigate?url=${STALL}/next
wait 2
cra://debug?captureToEasel=1
expect-log capture: the page didn't say where it is scrolled, sent without
wait 2
cra://debug?browserWindows=captured
expect-log browser windows captured: kind=normal listed=1 tabs=2 open=1
